= Asquith Resigns


After months of internal clashing within the liberal party, there was to be a motion to determine which of the two senior liberal figures would be party leader but tragedy occurs.

Days before the conference, Mr Asquith suffered a stroke, preventing him from attending. Leading to David Lloyd Goerge to claim victory be crowned party leader.
  
- @lloyd_george: Lloyd George is now the Liberal Party Leader


